<title>FRANCE: France to cut small, medium business taxes.</title>
<headline>France to cut small, medium business taxes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>French government spokesman Alain Lamassoure said the government intended to help small and medium-sized business in its 1997 budget by cutting taxes on their profits to 19 percent from 35 percent.</p>
<p>The government intended the move because small and medium-sized companies are &quot;job creators,&quot; Lamassoure, who is also budget minister, told radio station RTL.</p>
<p>He gave no further details.</p>
<p>The government is due to unveil its 1997 budget on September 18. It announced a variety of tax changes for 1997 last Thursday aimed at stimulating the economy.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
